        "As $\\alpha$ increases, probability mass spreads more evenly across the vocabulary.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Sentence probability and log-probability\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $w_{1:T}$ be a sentence after adding boundary tokens.  Under an $n$-gram model,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "p(w_{1:T})\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\prod_{t=n}^{T}p(w_t\\mid w_{t-n+1:t-1}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "In computation, we usually work with log-probabilities:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\log p(w_{1:T})\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\sum_{t=n}^{T}\\log p(w_t\\mid w_{t-n+1:t-1}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This is numerically more stable because products of many small probabilities can underflow to zero.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Python example: sentence log-probability"
      ],
      "id": "5cf37c0a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def sentence_logprob(sentence, n, vocab, context_counts, next_counts, alpha=0.5):\n",
        "    tokens = add_boundaries(tokenize(sentence), n)\n",
        "    d = len(vocab)\n",
        "    logp = 0.0\n",
        "    details = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i in range(n - 1, len(tokens)):\n",
        "        context = tuple(tokens[i - n + 1:i])\n",
        "        word = tokens[i]\n",
        "        count_context = context_counts[context]\n",
        "        count_pair = next_counts[context][word]\n",
        "        prob = (count_pair + alpha) / (count_context + alpha * d)\n",
        "        logp += math.log(prob)\n",
        "        details.append((context, word, prob))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return logp, details\n",
        "\n",
        "sentence = \"language models learn probability\"\n",
        "logp, details = sentence_logprob(sentence, 2, vocab, context_counts, next_counts, alpha=0.5)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Sentence:\", sentence)\n",
        "print(\"Log-probability:\", round(logp, 4))\n",
        "print(\"Probability:\", round(math.exp(logp), 8))\n",
        "print(\"\\nFactors:\")\n",
        "for context, word, prob in details:\n",
        "    print(f\"P({word:16s} | {context}) = {prob:.4f}\")"
      ],
